    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Common forms",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Lexical s-verbs can appear in tense forms like other verbs. The present tense, the form used for now or general statements, often looks the same as the infinitive for these verbs. The simple past, also called "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "preteritum",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", is especially important because several forms are common in everyday Bokmål."
            }
          ]
        },
